# Written by `vercel link`.
.vercel

# Every local env file, including the ones the rules further up miss
# (`.env.production`, `.env.staging`).
.env*
# …except the checked-in templates. This exception has to come *after* the
# pattern above, because the last matching rule wins — and `.env*` on its own
# silently overrode the `!.env.example` at the top of this file. Nothing broke
# today, since the two existing templates are already tracked, but a *new*
# `.env.example` would have refused to stage. CLAUDE.md §9 makes that file the
# first of the five places every new secret has to be written down, and the
# whole point of that checklist is that a missing entry is invisible until
# production is quietly running without the variable.
!.env.example
!*.env.example
